<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Medo-Babylonian conquest of the Assyrian Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">626–609 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Medo-Babylonian conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> was the war of 626–609 BCE in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabopolassar">Nabopolassar</a>, joined from 615 BCE by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyaxares">Cyaxares</a>, destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neo-assyrian-empire">Neo-Assyrian Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assur">Assur</a> fell in 614 BCE and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a> was sacked in 612 BCE; the last Assyrian king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashur-uballit-ii">Ashur-uballit II</a>, was defeated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harran">Harran</a> in 610–609 BCE. Assyria's lands were divided between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-empire">Neo-Babylonian Empire</a> and the Medes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/medo-babylonian-conquest-of-the-assyrian-empire.jpg" alt="Medo-Babylonian conquest of the Assyrian Empire" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ningyou · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Assyria.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
